@@ -0,0 +1,134 @@
+# WC3 Ability Completion — Temporary Patch Status
+
+This status accompanies `warcraft3-ability-completion.tmp.patch`. The patch is
+an implementation draft based on
+`warcraft3-ability-completion-implementation.tmp.md`. It is not a claim of
+complete retail parity. Tests and builds have not been run.
+
+## Included changes
+
+- Tighten Charm target validation and avoid dereferencing absent UnitBalance.
+  The stock ANch target outcomes are now verified in retail JASS: a level-3
+  neutral-hostile nftt transfers; an Hpal, a dead nftt corpse, and a live nftt
+  with permanent ACsk remain with Player 12. A follow-up boundary probe
+  confirms a level-5 stock-row override and custom organic levels 4–5
+  transfer, while level 6 remains with Player 12. The custom level-3 copy
+  anomalously stayed with Player 12; that result is unexplained. See the full
+  reproducible test
+  record in docs/games/warcraft-3/ability-verification-review.md.
+- Apply Purge's slow/stop only to hostile targets while retaining dispel and
+  summon damage behavior.
+- Track Faerie Fire's forced-vision contribution through status refresh,
+  expiry, dispel and death cleanup.
+- Add Shadow Strike initial damage, periodic status damage and a separately
+  timed movement/attack reduction.
+- Add Phoenix Fire passive target acquisition, direct damage and cooldown.
+- Give Immolation one status-backed toggle state, recurring mana drain and
+  ground-target damage pulses.
+- Mark Mirror Images with their source ability, avoid copying Hero ability
+  slots, and apply provisional illusion damage multipliers.
+- Read Engineering Upgrade movement and attack bonuses from authored data.
+- Stop routing Cluster Rockets through Flame Strike and defer its execution
+  with a diagnostic until its bombardment fields are understood.
+- Replace Carrion Swarm's point burst with an explicit diagnostic deferral
+  until travel and damage-cap behavior are understood.
+- Correct audited registry rows for Cluster Rockets, Serpent Ward, Charm,
+  Soul Preservation, and several stat item aliases.
+
+## Tooltip data verification (TFT AbilityData)
+
+`ability_audit -resolve-tooltip` was run on the listed stock rows. These
+values verify authored tooltip statements, not retail runtime timing, target
+filters, damage application, status ownership, or other hidden mechanics.
+
+- `AHre`: six friendly nearby corpses. `AIrs` item row separately has DataA=6
+  but no matching ability Ubertip; `APrl`/`APrr` are absent from AbilityData.
+- `AOmi`: creates 1/2/3 illusions by rank, dispels the Blademaster's magic,
+  lasts 60 seconds.
+- `ANch`: enemy target; excludes Heroes and creeps above level 5. Retail JASS
+  target observations are recorded separately below.
+- `AEim`/`ACim`: 10/15/20 DPS (hero ranks) and 10 DPS (creep row) against
+  nearby enemy land units; mana drains until deactivated.
+- `AUcs`: 75/125/200 to each enemy unit in a cone. Line rows describe enemy
+  land units: `ACca` 75 damage/300 maximum, `ACcv` and `ACc2` 150/900,
+  `ACc3` 100/300. `ACc1` has no AbilityData row.
+- `AOeq`: 50 building DPS, 75% slow, 25 seconds.
+- `AEsh`: initial 75/150/225; 10/30/45 every 3 seconds for 15.1 seconds;
+  movement slow only says “short duration.” `ACss`: 75 initial, 10 every 3
+  seconds for 15.1 seconds; attack and movement slow “short duration.”
+- `ANfa`: +5/10/15 attack damage; attack and movement slow 30/50/70%; 5 sec.
+- `ANcs` and `ANc1`–`ANc3`: “up to” 45/75/110 damage; stun 1.01 sec.
+- `ANeg`: +2/4/6 attack damage, +10/20/30% Tinker movement speed; improves
+  other Tinker abilities.
+- `Afae`: armor −4, gives vision, 90 sec. `ACff`: armor −4, gives vision,
+  30 sec.
+- `Arav`: changes Druid into flying Storm Crow. `Aro1`/`Aro2`: rooted Ancient
+  is immobile, can build, gives Protector thrown-rock attack, grants Fortified
+  armor. `Aroo` itself has no AbilityData tooltip row.
+- `Amfl`: +12 armor for 30 sec and describes damage when nearby enemies cast
+  spells. `ANms`: absorbs 1/1.5/2 damage per mana by rank.
+- `Apxf`: only says it fires flame streams and lights nearby enemies on fire;
+  tooltip provides no damage or timing values.
+
+`AIlp` has no AbilityStrings Ubertip in this install. Proposed stat rows
+`AIab`, `AInm`, and `AIgm` do not resolve as AbilityData tooltip entries;
+`AIrs` is a separate item-resurrection row and `AItm` resolves to the tome
+class/data without an ability tooltip. Continue those checks through
+ItemData, ItemStrings and parent/code aliases. Missing tooltip text is not
+evidence that the behavior or item is absent.
+
